ector.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"19d818f8ecdfc25e423979565165654df309e6994d6190fc58c5abe6c8e7304c"},"seconds":20.83758044242859,"seed":1020110604077344861,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\), where \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is a unit vector, we start by understanding the expression \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\). This expression represents the scalar triple product, which can be interpreted as the volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\). The maximum value of this scalar triple product occurs when \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is chosen such that \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is parallel to \\(\\mathbf{c}\\), and in that case, the value of the scalar triple product is the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) times the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the cross product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -10 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(4 \\cdot (-10) - 6 \\cdot (-7)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(-1 \\cdot (-10) - 6 \\cdot 2\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(-1 \\cdot (-7) - 4 \\cdot 2\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (-40 + 42) - \\mathbf{j} (10 - 12) + \\mathbf{k} (7 - 8) = 2\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nNext, we find the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + 2^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 4 + 1} = \\sqrt{9} = 3\n\\]\nThe magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + (-7)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 100} = \\sqrt{153} = 3\\sqrt{17}\n\\]\nThe maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is the product of the magnitudes of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\), since \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) are parallel when \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is chosen appropriately:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| \\cdot \\|\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c}\\| = 3\\sqrt{17} \\cdot 3 = 9\\sqrt{17}\n\\]\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is \\(\\boxed{9\\sqrt{17}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9\\sqrt{17}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:498"}
